1
00:04:44,444 --> 00:04:50,444
No one comes close to James Bond, 007.

2
00:09:28,888 --> 00:09:34,888
For Your Eyes Only is a adventure, action, thriller film directed by John Glen.

3
00:14:13,333 --> 00:14:19,333
A British spy ship has sunk and on board was a hi-tech encryption device.

4
00:18:57,777 --> 00:19:03,777
James Bond is sent to find the device that holds British launching
instructions before the enemy Soviets get to it first.

5
00:23:42,222 --> 00:23:48,222
James Bond, played by Roger Moore.

6
00:28:26,666 --> 00:28:32,666
Melina Havelock, played by Carole Bouquet.

7
00:33:11,111 --> 00:33:17,111
Milos Columbo, played by Chaim Topol.

8
00:37:55,555 --> 00:38:01,555
Aristotle Kristatos, played by Julian Glover.

9
00:42:40,000 --> 00:42:46,000
Bibi Dahl, played by Lynn-Holly Johnson.

10
00:47:24,444 --> 00:47:30,444
Countess Lisl von Schlaf, played by Cassandra Harris.

11
00:52:08,888 --> 00:52:14,888
For Your Eyes Only is a 1981 spy film, the twelfth film in the James Bond franchise produced by Eon
Productions, and the fifth to star Roger Moore as the fictional MI6 agent James Bond.

12
00:56:53,333 --> 00:56:59,333
The film also co-stars Carole Bouquet, Chaim Topol, Lynn-Holly Johnson and Julian Glover, and marked the feature directorial
debut of John Glen, who had served as a film editor and second unit director on previous films in the series.

13
01:01:37,777 --> 01:01:43,777
The film was written by Richard Maibaum and Michael G.

14
01:06:22,222 --> 01:06:28,222
Although the script is principally based on two Ian Fleming short stories, "For Your Eyes Only" and "Risico", some elements of
the plot were also inspired by the novels Live and Let Die, Goldfinger and On Her Majesty's Secret Service.

15
01:11:06,666 --> 01:11:12,666
The film follows Bond as he attempts to locate a missile command system while becoming tangled in a web of deception spun
by rival Greek smugglers along with Melina Havelock, a woman seeking to avenge the murder of her parents.

16
01:15:51,111 --> 01:15:57,111
After the science-fiction-focused Moonraker, the producers wanted a return to the
style of the early Bond films and the works of 007 creator Fleming.

17
01:20:35,555 --> 01:20:41,555
For Your Eyes Only followed a grittier, more realistic approach and a narrative theme of
revenge and its consequences, rather than the fantasy narrative of Moonraker.

18
01:25:20,000 --> 01:25:26,000
Filming took place from September 1980 to February 1981, and locations included Greece,
Italy and the United Kingdom, while underwater footage was shot in the Bahamas.

19
01:30:04,444 --> 01:30:10,444
Sheena Easton performed the title theme song.

20
01:34:48,888 --> 01:34:54,888
For Your Eyes Only was released in the UK on 24 June 1981 and in the US two
days later; it received a mixed-to-positive critical reception.

21
01:39:33,333 --> 01:39:39,333
The film's reputation has improved over time, with reviewers praising the more
serious tone in comparison to previous entries in the series.

22
01:44:17,777 --> 01:44:23,777
The film was a financial success, generating $195.3 million worldwide.

23
01:49:02,222 --> 01:49:08,222
For Your Eyes Only was the final Bond film to be distributed solely by United Artists; the
company was absorbed by Metro-Goldwyn-Mayer soon after this film's release.

24
01:53:46,666 --> 01:53:52,666
It was followed by Octopussy in 1983.

25
01:58:31,111 --> 01:58:37,111
The film explores themes of sea, assassin, london,
england, smuggling (contraband), submarine.

26
02:03:15,555 --> 02:03:21,555
The tone is intense.
